{
    "background_story": "Rosie was a brilliant artist, known for her vibrant paintings and whimsical sculptures. However, her creative genius was often overshadowed by her notorious absentmindedness. She would forget appointments, misplace her keys, and even leave her coffee brewing for hours. One day, Rosie became so engrossed in a new project that she forgot about a crucial art exhibition, where her work was supposed to be showcased. Panicked, she rushed to the gallery, only to realize she had left her paintings at home. Despite the chaos she often created, Rosie's art patrons and friends adored her, finding her forgetfulness charming and endearing. Her absentmindedness became an integral part of her quirky persona, and she learned to laugh at her own forgetfulness, often incorporating it into her art.",
